objectives.expectedResult:
National Federation Presidents, General Secretaries, and Coaches actively engage in structured capacity-building sessions and advance the development and implementation of key planning documents, including: 
• National Federation Multi-Cycle Operations, Shared Calendar & Participation Plan; 
• High Performance Annual Training Plans; 
• Athlete, Coach and Official Development Pathways; 
• Federation Multi-Cycle High Performance Plans; 
• School Visit Participation Plans and Olympic Month activities. 
• Federation leaders increase awareness of upcoming coach development opportunities offered by Panam Sport in partnership with Canada’s coaching program beginning in August and urged to contact olympic committee with expressions of interest,  strengthen communication with the Dominica Olympic Committee, and improve their capacity to plan, monitor, and coordinate federation activities.
• federation leaders become more engaged through contributions to Olympic Committee's June school visit presenation and/or Olympic Day demonstrations

National Federation Presidents, General Secretaries, and Coaches are formally engaged and reminded of outstanding planning and development requirements, including the identification of federation representatives to work with the Sport Methodologist on:

National Federation Multi-Cycle Operations, Shared Calendar, and Participation Plans;
Annual High Performance Training Plans;
Athlete, Coach, and Official Development Pathways;
Multi-Cycle High Performance Plans;
School Visit Participation Plans and Olympic Month activities.

National Federations are informed of available coach development opportunities and encouraged to identify suitable candidates for participation in Panam Sports, Olympic Solidarity, and Canadian coaching education programmes.

The Dominica Olympic Committee is encouraged to promote coach education opportunities through public communications and press releases to broaden awareness and attract interested applicants, including individuals not currently affiliated with National Federations.
